      "writtenOn": "2026-08-25T03:25:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The proposed condition works for the current default case, but could we make it more robust by checking whether `valid_status_codes` contains a successful status code instead of requiring the exact `[${HTTP_OK},${HTTP_NO_CONTENT}]` list?\n\nFor example, `Create LDAP Configuration` defaults to:\n\n```robotframework\n...  ${valid_status_codes}\u003d[${HTTP_OK},${HTTP_NO_CONTENT}]\n```\n\nbut callers may also use `[${HTTP_NO_CONTENT}]` for a successful update, for example:\n\n```robotframework\nCreate LDAP Configuration    valid_status_codes\u003d[${HTTP_NO_CONTENT}]\n```\n\nIn this case, the LDAP service may still need the 15-second restart wait.Therefore, the condition could be changed to:\n\n```robotframework\n${update_should_succeed}\u003d  Run Keyword And Return Status\n...  Should Contain Any  ${valid_status_codes}\n...  ${HTTP_OK}  ${HTTP_NO_CONTENT}\n\nIF  ${update_should_succeed}\n    Sleep  15s\nEND\n```",
      "range": {
