      "writtenOn": "2026-08-26T06:14:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Good catch @spotthur@in.ibm.com,\n\nActually, we need to order the Teardown like below,\n\n[Teardown] Run Keywords Redfish.Login AND\n... FFDC On Test Case Fail  AND\n... Create LDAP Configuration\n\nWe call FFDC On Test Case Fail before Create LDAP Configuration because FFDC only captures a live snapshot of current system state (logs, dumps, Redfish/AccountService data) — it can\u0027t retroactively capture what state existed at failure time.\n\nFor this test, we intentionally leave an invalid LDAP config in place to verify failure behavior. If we restore the config (Create LDAP Configuration) before running FFDC, and the test then fails unexpectedly, FFDC would collect logs from the already-restored/healthy state — not the actual invalid config that caused the failure. That makes the FFDC bundle useless for root-causing.\n\nSo the order should be: login (ensure valid session) → FFDC (diagnose actual failure state) → restore config (cleanup for next test).",
      "parentUuid": "ecd3f836_55095805",
